WEBVTT

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:04.880
Hinako is an elementary schooler whom I had just met.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.850
Even though she's only ten, she's already audacious and wants to be an adult.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.210
It's so much trouble because she said that she's in love with Shuu.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.830
Somehow, I got caught in the mess and I had to help out.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:24.370
I set up Shuu and Hinako to be alone together on a date at the aquarium to allow her to confess.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:29.780
And the result...? Well, I hope Hinako recovers quickly.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.000
Nanaka? It's me.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.490
Nanaka?

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.840
Yes!

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.120
How goes the dance practice?

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:02.350
I've almost got all the steps down. So, just a little more.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.960
I see. Keep up the good work then.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.580
There are only a few days left till the performance.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.460
Yes. I'll do my best.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.940
So, uncle, is that all?

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:19.000
It looks like we'll be using the bonfire lights for the dance stage.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.620
I just wanted to inform you.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.500
I see. Sorry for being so demanding.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.950
Not at all. On the contrary, I'm the one being demanding.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.190
If you'll excuse me, I'd like to resume my practice.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.430
I see, sorry for interrupting you.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.030
Not at all.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.900
The Unblooming Sakuras

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:51.290
Sign: Sakuranomori Prefectural High School

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:48.830
Karaoke?

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:51.970
Yep. We're headed to the karaoke box in front of the station now.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:52.970
You're coming, right?

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:53.930
I don't mind.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.240
I'm going too.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.770
What about you, Nanaka?

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.250
I'm sorry, but I can't go.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.390
I have to go home and practice.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.570
What practice?

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:07.270
You know. The Sakura Festival at the Yatsushiro Temple is coming soon.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.930
Nanaka will be performing the sakura dance.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.200
Sakura dance?

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.260
You don't remember, Sana-chan? 
We all watched it when we were kids.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:20.270
They would build a stage in front of the temple at the shrine and a Shinto priestess would dance.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.280
It was dark, but the bonfire lighting made it really beautiful.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:28.900
They haven't had a dance performance for over ten years.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.470
But they have Nanaka-chan this year!

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.400
Actually, I didn't really want to do it.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.070
But now, I'm under the care of my uncle, so I couldn't refuse.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:43.580
Oh yeah. Your uncle is the Shinto priest of Yatsushiro Temple.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:49.530
The priest there always looks so sullen. He's kinda scary, don't you think?

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:55.240
We did play a lot there last time, but I don't remember the priest ever saying a word.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.070
But Nanaka, why are you staying with your uncle?

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.420
It's because...

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.590
Well, there are reasons...

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.860
Hidaka-kun! Shopping?

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.510
Something like that. How about you, Hoshino-san?

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.440
I'm buying some magazines. And also...

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:24.370
Say, Hidaka-kun. Can you please accompany me for a bit?

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.730
You have a cat?

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.910
It's not mine; it belongs to the home.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.040
Home?

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:38.540
I do volunteer work at an old-folks home nearby my place once in a while.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:43.680
I make sure they keep themselves clean, and also talk to them.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:49.660
The other day, we found a lost cat over there and the home decided to keep him.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:54.540
I thought it'd be a good idea to give him a collar since he belongs to the home now.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.370
His name is Poe.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.580
I thought that I might have chosen something too cute...

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:03.830
...so I figured that it'd be better for you to choose.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:06.100
Well, if I can be of help.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:10.670
Say Hidaka-kun, why don't you come to the home this Saturday?

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:13.200
They wanted some help from a guy.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.040
Sure thing. I'm free on that day after all.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.960
Really? You'll be a great help!

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.060
Hmm, Nanaka?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.060
Sana, you're shopping with Hoshino-san?

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.070
I bumped into Hoshino-san over there earlier.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:45.380
And she wanted some help picking out a cat collar.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.780
I see, it was a coincidence...

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.090
Are you shopping too?

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.800
No, I had to run an errand for my uncle on my way back.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.980
That reminds me. This Saturday...

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:01.040
...I'm going to do volunteer work at the old-folks home with Hoshino-san.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.820
Would you like to come too, Nanaka?

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.590
Oh yeah. You have to practice your dance.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.110
I'll go.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.720
But, what about your practice?

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.600
It's okay. I've memorized most of it already.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.110
So, I'd like to come along.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.630
Mushou Academy Old Folks Home

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.650
Hello!

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:28.200
Welcome! Everyone's waiting for you.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.130
These are the ones I mentioned on the phone; Hidaka-kun and Yatsushiro-san.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:36.670
Thanks for coming. We're especially grateful to have a young man.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.340
Oh my, Poe. Did you come to greet me?

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.380
I've got a present for you today.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:55.720
That's nice. He looks more masculine now.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.550
Hidaka-kun picked it out, so make sure you thank him.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.920
This is the lounge.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.490
You're late!

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.840
Shuri?! Why are you here?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.410
Didn't Asami tell you?

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.030
Sorry, I forgot to tell them.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:21.090
Shuri became a volunteer first.
 She's the one who invited me to join.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.930
I see. So it's like that.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.980
They finally managed to get a boy?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.420
You're Shuri-chan's gaming partner, aren't you?

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.510
Gaming partner?

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:34.130
Lately, Yokoi-san has been engrossed in fighting games.

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:36.810
But, he's got no one to play with so it's a bit of a problem.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:40.370
What are you waiting for? Hurry and sit with me.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.460
Okay.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.680
Sorry for the trouble, but we're counting on you.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:48.740
<i>So this is what they wanted a guy for...</i>

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:53.120
I don't really like those old people 
stereotype games like Go and Shougi.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:55.980
Here I go!

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.030
Feel my sudden combo!

00:06:58.030 --> 00:06:59.620
Hey, where's Pi-chan?

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.830
It disappeared a while back.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:08.580
It probably escaped because the door latch came loose.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:09.840
Who's Pi-chan?

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:14.070
It's a Java sparrow. It was really friendly with people, and very adorable.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:17.430
Poe! You weren't the one who did it, right?

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.610
He said, “no.”

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:28.380
It's been so long since the last sakura dance. I'm really looking forward to it!

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:35.160
I don't see Kaji-san around.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:41.020
Grandma Kaji has a slight cold. She doesn't have a fever but she said she feels lethargic.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.760
That's worrying.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:46.340
Well, I'm sure she'll recover from the cold quickly.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.800
But, what I'm worried more about is her heart.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.530
Heart?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.280
Well, I guess it's not a disease.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:08:00.470
After Grandma Kaji lost her grandchild early this year, she's been acting strangely.

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:04.480
There was once when I took my eyes off her for a while and she suddenly disappeared.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.180
I'm not sure what she did or where she went,

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:10.100
but when she got back, both her hands were covered in mud.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:15.200
I take care of her the best I can, but sometimes I let my guard down too.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.520
Why don't you go visit her later?

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.290
I'm sure she'll be happy.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.490
Sure.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.410
Yes, please come in.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:28.920
Kaji-san, how are you feeling?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.650
I'm feeling much better now.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:35.130
You should have come and joined us at the lounge then.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:42.940
Hoshino-san and Wakatsuki-san came to see you. And their friends too.

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:44.940
They want to greet you.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:48.690
Oh my, how polite. Please come in.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:50.390
We're coming in.

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:52.180
Are you feeling all right?

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:56.330
Sorry to worry you all. It's really nothing serious.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:59.320
Let me introduce you. This is...

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.450
Motoko!

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.250
You came home!

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:16.410
Kaji-san, what's the matter? Please come to your senses.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.250
She's not your deceased granddaughter!

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.500
Kaji-san, are you okay?

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:28.530
Yes, I'm feeling okay now.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:30.800
Come, take a seat.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:36.800
Please forgive me for losing myself back there.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.460
It's just that you looked so much like Motoko.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.910
No, I don't mind.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:47.120
At the beginning of the year, Kaji-san lost her granddaughter in a car accident.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:52.060
She was pretty and had long hair. 
But, she didn't look exactly like you.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:54.600
But, there certainly are similarities.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.060
Mokoto was a gentle and sweet girl.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:02.390
As a child, she played the violin and she was really good.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:06.760
Your late granddaughter could play the violin too?

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:10.260
“Too”? You mean you can play the violin too?

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:11.840
Yeah.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:15.510
That's right. Motoko started in elementary school.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.930
And, she's even participated in several contests.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:22.600
That violin there is a memento.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:26.060
Because I was so saddened by the loss of my grandchild,

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:30.040
my daughter told me to keep it as a reminder of her.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:36.380
Nanaka, why don't you play something?

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.850
What are you saying?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:46.180
It's a precious memento. She wouldn't possibly let her play it.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:50.340
It's fine. Please play something for us.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:51.390
Yatsushiro-san.

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:52.440
Please.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.430
I'm sorry!

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.410
Nanaka, just play a little bit for Kaji-san.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:03.680
Sana!

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.840
Here is fine.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:20.130
Nanaka, I'm sorry about the violin thing earlier.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:25.510
I don't really understand. But, it seems that I thoughtlessly asked you to do that.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.070
If it's about that, I'm okay.

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:33.830
You didn't do anything wrong, so don't worry.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:34.960
But...!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.860
It's okay. Really.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.600
Nanaka!

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:42.140
Thank you for seeing me home. See you tomorrow.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.400
Sana-chan! I've come to fetch you!

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.300
Coming!

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.900
Aoi-chan, you're wearing a yukata.

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.880
Yep! Since it's the festival after all.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.310
How do I look?

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:13.460
You look great.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:15.910
So, let's get going, shall we?

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:29.210
Ah, here they are.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:30.260
Yes!

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.710
Sorry, did we make you wait long?

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.810
We just got here too.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:37.220
Aoi-chan is in a yukata.

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:41.200
Yep. Sana-chan just told me that I look great!

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:48.600
Since when did the unpleasant Sana-kun learn to praise a girl's clothes?

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.390
You're getting better!

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:53.010
What are you saying? I'm not like that!

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:55.640
Hey, quit dilly-dallying or else we'll leave you behind.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:58.090
We'll leave you behind!

00:12:58.350 --> 00:12:59.650
They're really excited.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:06.270
Say Shuu, wouldn't it have been better to meet up a little later?

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:09.810
Nanaka's sakura dance only starts when it gets dark, right?

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:15.500
That's right. But, I was so excited thinking about the festival while at home that I just couldn't keep still.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:19.440
Yeah, he was making such a commotion ever since he woke up in the morning.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.760
He's like a child holding his pee.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.600
What the hell is that?

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:32.020
You guys are slow!

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:33.920
When the heck did she...

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:37.290
Aoi-chan is really fast at times like these.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.090
We can't be beaten either.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.500
Sana, I challenge you to this one first!

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.510
Will you be able to defeat me?

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.030
I'm going to do a shrine prayer!

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:53.740
Yeah, since we're here already.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.400
Thank you very much.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.240
Hey, it's Nanaka.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:58.120
Sana.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.560
All of you came.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:04.680
Don't you have to prepare for the sakura dance?

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:10.230
I do. But there's still a lot of time before the rituals begin, so I'm helping out here.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.680
Sounds rough.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.430
We're going ahead.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:15.000
Okay, got it.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:17.230
What's that?

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:22.350
I won this at the rifle game. But, it's kinda hard to carry around.

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:23.860
What should I do with it?

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:25.460
I see.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.910
Shuri and Aoi-chan don't seem interested.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:32.630
Then, could I...

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.660
It's Yeti-kun!

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:41.510
Oh yeah. Hinako, you're collecting goods of this character, right?

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:42.300
Yeah.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:43.880
Here, a present.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.060
Is it okay?

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:47.200
It's no use for me to carry it around.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.040
How lucky!

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:54.290
So furry! This is what you call encouragement!

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:57.750
I've made up my mind! Can I have a festival charm please?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:58.750
Yes!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.330
You seem busy, so I'll look for you later.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.880
I'll be looking forward to your sakura dance.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.720
Sana, quickly, let's do the shrine prayer.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:08.770
Look what I got!

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.650
That's nice.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.610
So, they added those lights this time.

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.930
It's really pretty!

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:51.950
By the way, Sana-kun, do you know about the legend of the Twin Hills?

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:58.470
Yeah. If the sakuras bloom on the elder and younger sister hills, then your wish would come true, right?

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:01.750
And what's the reason behind the sakura dance?

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:06.390
Hmm, does that have anything to do with the legend of the Twin Hills?

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:08.310
Of course it does.

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:14.480
Originally, the sakura dance was a prayer for the sakuras to bloom on the Twin Hills.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:18.600
It was a offering so that wishes would come true.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:26.340
Actually, long ago, it was believed that they offered humans instead of a dance.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.560
Humans?

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:30.360
Yes. In other words, human sacrifices.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:34.210
Long, long ago, in order to make the sakuras bloom on either hill...

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:41.870
...they would bury people alive at the base of the largest sakura trees on each respective hill annually.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.660
I've heard of it too!

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:47.690
After they dug up the younger sister hill to erect the school,

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.400
they found a lot of human bones!

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:55.870
You're lying! If it's true, then I can't go to school from tomorrow onwards!

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:58.670
It's just a rumour.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:03.830
Don't be silly. Even if they did bury bones there, nothing would happen.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:07.290
As expected, Hinako really is mature.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.450
<i>He doesn't even mean it though.</i>

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:16.740
It's kinda unexpected that you're so 
knowledgeable about this, Shuri.

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:20.940
Hey, what do you mean by unexpected?

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:24.880
Well, I mean it's just unexpected.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.360
That's all?

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:32.800
Actually, this story was passed down from Grandma Kaji.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:34.150
So, that's why.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:38.760
Grandma Kaji's husband passed away a long time ago.

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:42.030
I guess you could call it local history.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:45.260
He researched the ancient customs of the town.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:49.460
And naturally, Grandma Kaji became very knowledgeable in that area too.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.690
Look!

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:55.990
It's starting!

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:41.570
So, here you are.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:45.420
You okay? You look kinda tired.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:47.870
Yeah, a little.

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:52.290
How was my dance? Was it strange?

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.530
It was incredibly beautiful!

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:00.340
It was like surreal or something.

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:02.350
I felt like I fell into a trance watching.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.250
Thank you.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:12.280
What are you doing after this? Would you like to visit the stalls with everyone?

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:14.730
But haven't you all seen everything already?

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:17.580
Yeah, we have...

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:22.450
I just wanted everyone gathered to see the sights like last time.

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:32.230
Hey, what's wrong?

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:36.260
Something brushed past my leg just now and ran over there.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:45.800
Look carefully.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:50.780
A raccoon.

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:55.990
I'm having a little trouble breathing with you clenching me so hard.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:00.710
I'm sorry!

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:01.850
Not at all.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:17.910
Everyone... 
-Umm...

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.050
Sorry.

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:21.100
Not at all, me too.

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:42.100
So here you are!

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:51.420
<i>Next, at the Yatushiro Temple in the Sakuranomori district...</i>

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:55.580
<i>...brought back after ten-odd years, the Shinto ritual, the sakura dance.</i>

00:20:55.580 --> 00:21:01.350
<i>This is the legend of the Twin Hills, where your dreams will come true if the sakuras bloom on the hills.</i>

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:06.080
<i>So that the sakuras may blossom on the Twin Hills this year...</i>

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:12.070
<i>...the Yatsuhiro Temple offers the ancient dance.</i>

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:15.880
<i>Recently, there had been no dancers, thus the performance was cancelled...</i>

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:17.980
<i>...but this year, it has made a come-back.</i>

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:21.130
<i>For over ten years...</i>

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.900
In the anticipated next episode;

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:31.840
you'll be seeing plenty of air-time from my mature self!

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:37.840
Under one roof, a sexy elementary school girl and an unmanageable high school boy...

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:43.000
Next time on Myself; Yourself:
I'm an Adult.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.190
Non-adult viewers, please watch secretly!

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:48.900
Sana-chan, as I thought, you're <i>that</i> kinda person...

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:50.300
I'm not!

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:55.070
I'm an Adult

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:54.810
This is a wholesome love comedy. There are no weird scenes!
